{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246887-isekai-the-thrill-of-power-and-exalted","id":1246887,"title":"Isekai, the Thrill of Power, and Exalted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-16T22:47:24-07:00","id":1246887,"title":"Isekai, the Thrill of Power, and Exalted","content":"&quot;Nearly all men can withstand adversity, but if you want to test a man's character, give him power.&quot; -Abraham Lincoln<br /> <br /> This quote is at the start of the 3ed Exalted Core, and i love it. Exalted are truly larger than life, and the stories they can have should shake the world.<br /> <br /> Isekai is a genre of Japanese Anime thay is quite big at the moment. It means 'another world', and includes very numerous shows about regular people going to a fantasy realm. Lately these anime include two things: the worlds being video games/rpgs, and the main character being WAAAYYY overpowered.<br /> <br /> This can bore some people at first, but it lets a very important thing happen in these shows and can help in Exalted games. It lets players have an easy start as they learn how this different world works. The player decides if they obey the rule of the land or threatens it. Relationships made are far more important and can get more dramatic. And by having the first sets of fights be almost underwhelming, players realize they can do more, and then the scope of action can go up and up.<br /> <br /> It also showcases what a party can do together well. Using modern tactics or concepts is not bad roleplaying, it can be a perk. The badguys know they can't fight the Dawn Caste, so they send their seduction assassins. Too bad the Eclipse and Night Caste members regularly screen new hires.<br /> <br /> What else can help a game of Exalted with this source material in mind? What pitfalls need to be avoided? I mean beyond the bad habits of these becoming Harem anime too often due to them not having good reasoning for making a party of characters beyond all of one gender chasing a single leader? Being overpowered demigods doesn't always need an equal challenge off the bat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T05:00:18-07:00","id":1246963,"title":"","content":"I think for an Isekai level of game, you'd really need to discuss things with your players first and often. Maybe you could get away with the first session or two being a surprise as the Circle discovers that they stand alone at their own level. I suspect that without some shared ideas about what to engage with, such a story would become rudderless and lost.<br /> <br /> A couple of examples...<br /> <br /> <i>Overlord </i>has Momonga realizing that his mental self is not as cool as his character self. Also because of his love for his guild and underlings he chooses to very cautiously explore the new world. He could stomp on just about any problem, but chooses to delegate -- all the while encouraging his underlings to grow. He could be a great example of the kind of Solaroid you'd want to swear to, if you were a Terrestrial-level in search of work. <br /> <br /> <i>Starting from Zero in Another World</i> has a limited sort of Isekai power-trip going on, in that Subaru has many chances to figure out problems but he's not especially powerful intrinsically. I think it might be a good story seed for a Sidereals game - instead of Return by Death, you'd lose a Resplendent Destiny and re-enter the story with a new one.<br /> <br /> <i>Knights &amp; Magic</i> would be a good example of planning out story ideas with a player. Ernesti could have blown away the power and rulership of the world, but instead all of the maneuvering of power and empire happens as a backdrop. Isekai Twilight who appears among a Gens of warstrider technicians?<br /> <br /> There are several recent or ongoing ones where the Isekai exile protagonist chooses to lay low in order to enjoy the situation. To be honest, they run together in my mind, so I don't even recall their names right away. There's that one with the demon lord character, the one with the programmer who fell asleep, that other one with that guy who did that thing, blah blah blah. What they have in common is that they're written with the knowledge that the protagonist is going to choose to explore the setting without exposing their power. That's a good example of discussing the expectation with your players first - so you can write adventures where they pretend to be average or average-good, but have a few opportunities to unleash full power at critical moments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T14:22:27-07:00","id":1247166,"title":"","content":"Isekai is a terrible genre that's literally selfinsert marysue fiction. It all revolves around one person who's better than anyone despite just dying to a japanese truck. You'd have to get a group is not only okay with seceding all limelight to one character who is better than everyone, but also be okay with the fact that said MC is going to be the only focus in the series. If you couldn't tell, yeah I think isekai is garbage. I wouldn't add into the game at all especially not without talking to the group.<br /> <br /> Edit-the issue with the genre in exalted is that it inherently makes the character more special than anyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 08-17-2018, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T14:39:02-07:00","id":1247172,"title":"","content":"Blatant wish fulfilment fantasy that begins with the self insert being hit by a truck sounds like a bit of a cry for help to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T17:00:16-07:00","id":1247228,"title":"","content":"There are quite a few classic isekai anime series, which are pretty good in and of themselves, but also that served as important sources of inspiration for Exalted back when it was first being written and developed - Magic Knights Rayearth, Vision of Escaflowne (Warstriders were directly inspired by Guymelefs), El-Hazard, and plenty of others. I even seem to remember Grabowski mentioning Those Who Hunt Elves once in a conversation.<br /> <br /> Back during First Edition I ran a couple of campaigns with that concept - the players were characters from Earth who were transported to Creation, given Exaltations and told to save the world. It's not an uncommon trope (The Lion the Witch and Wardrobe is pretty well known after all) and it's easy enough to pull off with Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-17-2018, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T18:07:05-07:00","id":1247249,"title":"","content":"Hmm, i think my focus got missed for what bits are inspiring.<br /> <br /> The game should have all the PCs as Main characters. All of them are Exalted, and all are superhuman. Solars most of all. Gate was an Isekai where Japan counter invaded a fantasy realm. In that realm was a demigod of war or death or something. Very Solar Exalted-esque, not the main person.<br /> <br /> Coming from another world is not the main idea (unless you want to run that game), but it is instead being thrust into that power that those insert plots usually give to main PCs. A cellphone with Google search and Maps can be mimicked with good survival, awareness and lore. It is actually enjoying and being amazed by that. Maybe describe an amazing awareness roll like suddenly feeling everyone at once like on a map.<br /> <br /> And as PCs, the group collectively are the most important people in Creation. Especially fitting for Solars, mysterious powerful people just appearing out of nowhere. Blowing through 'typical' challenges, until all of the ancient powers that felt they ran everything suddenly see you on their radars and realize that whatever they planned millenia for did not account for the party.<br /> <br /> Cut out all the bad genre flaws. The bad harem design is half there for self insert wish fulfillment and half there as a poor way to bring a party together. Unless you want inter PC romance, cut that junk out. Let PCs get a taste of what they do with power, but after a couple of sessions, give them the consequences for those actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24220,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","user":"Cryo-Seraph","date":". 08-17-2018, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T18:25:23-07:00","id":1247252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cryo-Seraph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246887-isekai-the-thrill-of-power-and-exalted?p=1247249#post1247249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A cellphone with Google search and Maps can be mimicked with good survival, awareness and lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a pretty big difference between knowing something and knowing how to look something up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T18:58:38-07:00","id":1247261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246887-isekai-the-thrill-of-power-and-exalted?p=1247252#post1247252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a pretty big difference between knowing something and knowing how to look something up.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was just an example riffing off of the anime with a cellphone for his special power. The idea is more that rolling a full excellency on a strong dice pool action will be as amazing as what a medieval fantasy character hears when someone googles an answer. Instant knowledge from a super-genius. 10-20 successes is nutso crazy when most challenges in the game are diff 1-5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T18:21:50-07:00","id":1247572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246887-isekai-the-thrill-of-power-and-exalted?p=1247172#post1247172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blatant wish fulfilment fantasy that begins with the self insert being hit by a truck sounds like a bit of a cry for help to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I think its pretty big cry for help when one of the biggest genres right now is when your life is so bad it takes killing you to put you in an ideal world.<br /> <br /> I think the strengths of Isekai are the fact that its relatable. Not only to the characters (Ever wonder why so many of them are ex-gamers?) but also in a deeper sense. They're a fish out of the water and they're learning the world alongside the reader themselves. This is why many movie often have a young apprentice who is ignorant about the world at large in the movies as well. Luke Skywalker in part 4 is an excellent example of this. Frodo in Lord of the Rings is another example of this, taken along in an epic jounrey despite Gandalf being a literal angel who is far stronger but serves as a mentor figure.<br /> <br /> Can Exalted pull of the Isekai genre? Absolutely, I toyed with the idea myself (Personally I think modern has it covered better but that's a tangent). Its a good way to get the players introduced in the setting if they know nothing of it. If you're perfectly happy with the idea then go for it.<br /> <br /> I'd make all the players play familiar with Tabletop RPG's and have a charm which allows them to see their own statsheet too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T19:18:05-07:00","id":1247587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cryo-Seraph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246887-isekai-the-thrill-of-power-and-exalted?p=1247249#post1247249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, i think my focus got missed for what bits are inspiring.<br /> <br /> The game should have all the PCs as Main characters. All of them are Exalted, and all are superhuman. Solars most of all. Gate was an Isekai where Japan counter invaded a fantasy realm. In that realm was a demigod of war or death or something. Very Solar Exalted-esque, not the main person.<br /> <br /> Coming from another world is not the main idea (unless you want to run that game), but it is instead being thrust into that power that those insert plots usually give to main PCs. A cellphone with Google search and Maps can be mimicked with good survival, awareness and lore. It is actually enjoying and being amazed by that. Maybe describe an amazing awareness roll like suddenly feeling everyone at once like on a map.<br /> <br /> And as PCs, the group collectively are the most important people in Creation. Especially fitting for Solars, mysterious powerful people just appearing out of nowhere. Blowing through 'typical' challenges, until all of the ancient powers that felt they ran everything suddenly see you on their radars and realize that whatever they planned millenia for did not account for the party.<br /> <br /> Cut out all the bad genre flaws. The bad harem design is half there for self insert wish fulfillment and half there as a poor way to bring a party together. Unless you want inter PC romance, cut that junk out. Let PCs get a taste of what they do with power, but after a couple of sessions, give them the consequences for those actions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think if your going for &quot;Insane power compared to other normal groups&quot; You could do it a couple ways.<br /> a N/A artifact might work--they are story warping, and by definition will make players powerful.<br /> Give them just more merit points.<br /> Have all of them find those...new destiny robots...devil stones? I think? That can grant incredible power!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T22:39:20-07:00","id":1247620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246887-isekai-the-thrill-of-power-and-exalted?p=1247572#post1247572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. I think its pretty big cry for help when one of the biggest genres right now is when your life is so bad it takes killing you to put you in an ideal world.<br /> <br /> I think the strengths of Isekai are the fact that its relatable. Not only to the characters (Ever wonder why so many of them are ex-gamers?) but also in a deeper sense. They're a fish out of the water and they're learning the world alongside the reader themselves. This is why many movie often have a young apprentice who is ignorant about the world at large in the movies as well. Luke Skywalker in part 4 is an excellent example of this. Frodo in Lord of the Rings is another example of this, taken along in an epic jounrey despite Gandalf being a literal angel who is far stronger but serves as a mentor figure.<br /> <br /> Can Exalted pull of the Isekai genre? Absolutely, I toyed with the idea myself (Personally I think modern has it covered better but that's a tangent). Its a good way to get the players introduced in the setting if they know nothing of it. If you're perfectly happy with the idea then go for it.<br /> <br /> I'd make all the players play familiar with Tabletop RPG's and have a charm which allows them to see their own statsheet too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think there's a lot to this. <br /> <br /> That said, I don't think you have to take the entire body of isekai tropes together. I'd look to this sort of show for inspiration, when it comes to Celestials dealing with once-friend mortals who grow increasingly distant (and relatively fragile) with their growing powers.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T01:27:59-07:00","id":1247640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cryo-Seraph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246887-isekai-the-thrill-of-power-and-exalted#post1246887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What else can help a game of Exalted with this source material in mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably the manner in which other people become invested in them and trying to harness or direct their abilities, particularly in terms of educating them about the wider political and social dynamics of a setting.<br /> <br /> Even if a player character is an actual native of the setting, I would say that enough Exalted come from humble or isolated backgrounds as to warrant that experience.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T03:48:19-07:00","id":1247658,"title":"","content":"On the genre, well, it's all down to the skill of the writer really; the Wizard Knight by Gene Wolfe is basically isekai in the terms provided, and it's awesome. And there are lots of other shows and movies within anime in this pedigree which are generally acknowledged as good stuff; 12 Kingdoms for ex. (And hilarously awful stuff like Garzey's Wing). This kind of secondary world fantasy featuring a young protagonist who shifts world has always been popular as I see it, as AnubisXY notes.<br /> <br /> (Of course, yeah, the modern trend has been to gradually amp with the power of anime protagonists, and then recently to parody this and show how power doesn't solve your life. Particularly in One's shows (though not isekai), which find the most inspiring and empathy inspiring characters are guys like Mumen Rider or Reigen who have absolutely no power whatsoever, and who are contrasted to shallow, power focused characters who lack development as mature adults, and where the shows as a whole a consistent message of critiquing a worldview based on accumulating power).<br /> <br /> But I do think that it's a bit opposite to what Exalted sets out to do, which is about playing characters who are generally formed and limited really by their experience in the game's world, despite their power? Less than turning up from the modern world with your boomstick and charisma and leading the masses of primitive screwheads with your modern strategy and knowledge. Of course you can change this in your game. Or you can make some analogies with how outsider native characters might play out. <br /> <br /> (The most straightforward iteration of the Fish-Out-of-Water from a modern culture in 2e was the First Age Survivor, who'd entered the setting equivalent of a cryo-tube only to awaken in the Age of Sorrows. This is less of thing given the First Age as implied by 3e so far! But you can perhaps do it to some extent still.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T04:04:25-07:00","id":1247659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246887-isekai-the-thrill-of-power-and-exalted?p=1247658#post1247658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the First Age Survivor, who'd entered the setting equivalent of a cryo-tube only to awaken in the Age of Sorrows. This is less of thing given the First Age as implied by 3e so far!</div> </div> </div> </div>You could do that with that veil that preserves something against the passage of time, or Dragon Blooded petrification magic, I think.<br /> <br /> I say &quot;I thing&quot;, because I can't remember the precise parameters of those magics, but I think they could manage it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T16:14:30-07:00","id":1248548,"title":"","content":"Also, here's an idea; let's have another isekai protagonist or group as the main villains, because the ability to indulge their fantasies has gone to their heads. These are the kind of people who throw tantrums when the world refuses to revolve around them or they face setbacks, or who view their harems as status symbols more than people. Or set out to build harems, and not in the fun, caring way that Issei does in <i>High School DxD </i>where it's clear he's fully aware that he needs to be perfectly honest about it and give as much as he takes. Some of them can be really sympathetic, too, the kind who want to create an industrial revolution but don't realize internal combustion doesn't function the same way in Creation, or that they need to figure out the printing press first, or keep a collar on the Guild so they don't turn cyberpunk with this new technology. <br /> <br /> Exalted is the prime place to examine internal problems of the genre and develop a way the main character contrasts said problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T18:46:07-07:00","id":1248592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246887-isekai-the-thrill-of-power-and-exalted?p=1248548#post1248548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exalted is the prime place to examine internal problems of the genre and develop a way the main character contrasts said problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! This and the idea of what an Isekai villainous person would actually do. That is the intriguing stuff to me. Anu Ecalted villain can have these things to a degree. Someone treated as a god is heady stuff, and staying focused on a 'good task' is tough with thungs to tempt and distract. Use them as foils to the charactera. If one PC likes the Cult Merit. Show them what a corrupt city god is like, and see if they take it as lesson learned or an example to follow.<br /> <br /> No one ever said PCs stay good guys too after all. Straying into Abyssals and the like eventually means you won't even start as one. Test PCs with what power really feels like. If no one in town can survive standing up to you without getting beat to a pulp, emphasize the fear they strike into even friendly allies. If they can make fortunes easy, only the money grubbers want to be their friends, who push the honest folk away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T08:10:09-07:00","id":1250452,"title":"","content":"Games with Isekai characters don't need to focus on the genre. You could, but it isn't necessary.<br /> My groups Twilight was from Earth and despite this he didn't like being in the limelight, in fact the only times he did so was to tell stories from his world to the Dawn, who took to using earth terms and phrases to other people. The kind that didn't make sense to anyone, even the Twilight.<br /> So yeah it can be done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23779-genericmalenpc01","name":"GenericMaleNPC01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T08:58:36-07:00","id":1250461,"title":"","content":"Oh hell. I just remembered. Remember the time Death talked about justice and mercy and duty? <br /> <br /> I think that would be a pretty good stunt, to do. I mean, there's no actual objective morality in exalted. This is pretty nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T10:42:48-07:00","id":1250483,"title":"","content":"12 Kingdoms was one of the things that got me into Exalted back in the day.<br /> <br /> I would be wary of criticizing Mary Sue author/reader insert fiction, overpowered characters or regular characters who for some reason gain the sudden loyalty of a bunch of cool sexy magic badasses are as old as storytelling itself. There's nothing wrong with a bit of escapism in fiction, and nothing wrong with stories about that escapism being literal trips to other worlds.<br /> <br /> Bilbo is a random bloke who is abruptly whisked off to a world of adventure by a bunch of cool mysterious strangers where he unexpectedly saved the day repeatedly. John Carter of Mars takes a nap and wakes up in a world where he's incredibly powerful and the princesses are nudists. The kids in Narnia wander into another world where they're quasi-sacred just for being humans, and where God Himself shows up to hang out with them and help them take over the place. Pern starts out with an unhappy scullery-slave getting whisked off by a dashing sky-knight because she has telepathic potential and getting a pet dragon. Ancient Egyptian pharoahs literally planned to go to a new world and rule over it after they got hit by trucks. <br /> <br /> Nothing about this kind of story is any less worthy than some other story structure, and I often feel that criticism of escapist otherworld stories or relatable-protagonist-becoming-poweful-or-popular stories focus on genre instead of the story's actual merits or flaws.<br /> <br /> Avant-Garde is bullshit, there is nothing new under the Sun, and something is not bad just because it has been done before. Ask why it is done so often, and whether this effort was done well, and your criticism will actually have some merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T01:28:10-07:00","id":1250680,"title":"","content":"So when I first saw this thread topic I'd actually thought of it in a bit of a different way. Basically as opposed to person from our world reborn in Creation and becoming an exalt, I'd been thinking we were going to discuss the idea of an exalt getting reborn into a different world. <br /> <br /> I mean a lot of these treat the reincarnation as a pretty continuous process, so you could use that as the handwave for why the circle are still exalted despite the normal part where death ends exaltation. It just seems like an interesting setup since you have the basics of the circle dealing with the new world and how their powers interact with it. Then you have stuff like this world responding to the power of the exalts, are the exalts power houses matched by few if any entities or are they closer to the mid tier. Heck does an exalt using an excellency get recognized as just a weird buff spell or freaking alien? Not to mention the circle potentially developing the concern on what happens if they die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T14:44:36-07:00","id":1251497,"title":"","content":"Self-Insert fanfiction is something I've seen a lot of, lately, and more than a bit of it is rather self-aware. Once or twice, I've seen stories where the SI'd author-avatar actually just replaced a canon character. Bam, opened his eyes, realized he's Iolus in Hercules: Legendary Journeys, or Lexington in Gargoyles, or something like that.<br /> <br /> Doing that with canon characters and your players could be interesting. &quot;Okay, guys, you've chosen the canon characters you want to play. But here's the twist: You don't have any of their memories or experiences, though you can access their skills and knowledge as represented by any stats or skills they have. Instead, you have your memories and personality. You've essentially just possessed them.&quot;<br /> <br /> So when your party is made up of Mnemon, Octavian, the Bull of the North, and Fokuf, but you're not even asking Jaime, Steve, Mark, and Frank to RP those characters, but rather themselves suddenly being in those characters' positions with everybody around them thinking they're those characters, what kind of game does that create? (Well, first, I suppose, as ST, you'd best contrive a way for them to be in touch with each other, or all in the same place!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}